The PR changes the team-access filter from chained `.filter()` calls to a single combined `Q` object. This is a security fix, not a regression: the base code's chained filters (`filter(teams__members=user).filter(teams__access=ADMIN_ACCESS)`) created two separate joins, which could return projects where the user is a member of one team but the access-level condition matched a different team on the same project — a privilege-escalation bug. The PR consolidates both conditions into one `Q` object so they apply to the same join, and the PR's own comment (lines 66-70) documents this. The change narrows (corrects) the authorization set rather than widening it, and the `exclude()` is applied to the same queryset. No new authorization flaw is introduced.

